  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "owned-session-pgid-cleanup",
      "severity": "major",
      "disposition": "fixed",
      "reason": "The baseline helper observed and killed only the outer PGID, so real Ninja rule shell/leaf processes in another PGID but the same owned SID remained alive after cleanup=complete. The final helper observes the owned session, retains the unreaped Popen leader identity, opens pidfds and rechecks PID/SID/starttime before signalling, then checks live members and stream/leader completion conservatively. The unchanged original 0.2-second probe independently observed the formerly omitted sh/leaf, preserved the timeout, and found no live leaf or need for independent cleanup after return. Its original expected-defect oracle exit 1/not-confirmed is retained; the preregistered reviewer harness separately passed."
    },
    {
      "id": "late-status-timeout-preservation",
      "severity": "major",
      "disposition": "fixed",
      "reason": "The first implementation could let a late process_status RuntimeError replace the original timeout and prevent fallback. The implementer preserved an actual RED using a real process and a narrow diagnostic-read failure. The final frozen helper treats that failure as session-unverified, preserves timeout and output, and retains the bounded original-group fallback while rejecting an observed replacement identity. The exact-source final module passed 52 tests with no skips, including this regression. The reviewer independently inspected the original RED, corrective diff and final source."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is an owner-delegated independent AI source review, not human review, field verification, provider execution or release authorization. Helper author is ai/implement-session-cleanup; the coordinator authored requirements/design, version metadata and evidence packaging. This reviewer did not modify the implementation, tests, requirements or design.",
    "The tested product is 5ff076a14c88c65132e44dd8bfdb4c2ab71ee4f8 / tree 14e5482c9ea3f97abe6abfcc74f8251088e46e8e. Subsequent evidence and normal review/archive output is a separately reviewed packaging overlay, not a claim that it was present during the clean full suite.",
    "Both original hosted main 15fa31d1 ADC/CMake 15-second timeouts remain UNKNOWN and outside the fixed findings. No attempt 3 of run 44116100760 was performed. Cleanup executes after TimeoutExpired, so this source fix and a new-head pass do not establish that the historical wait was cured or that runtime performance or stability improved.",
    "The helper owns the SID created by start_new_session and retains bounded diagnostics: 50 ms, 256 scanned entries, 16 records, with one shared 1-second cleanup deadline and the original 15-second default work budget. Missing, inaccessible or truncated observations and missing pidfd capabilities cannot certify complete. Deliberate setsid escape is outside this finite helper guarantee.",
    "Independent probes used actual local Ninja 1.11.1.git.kitware.jobserver-1 and actual pidfd operations on test-owned processes. No actual PID reuse, hosted Ninja binary equivalence, arbitrary process-tree containment or non-Linux full behavior was demonstrated. Forged SID/starttime and missing-capability branch scopes are explicit in retained raw results.",
    "The original immutable probe was designed to confirm the old defect, so its new-source exit 1/not-confirmed is retained without relabelling. The independent preregistered outer harness separately verified timeout preservation, snapshot membership, no live leaf, no extra cleanup, and unaffected unrelated-session controls, and exited 0.",
    "Frozen review-input-state and wrapper origin/source_directory values describe the historical observation location. Record-relative evidence survives normal archive moves; those original bytes must not be rewritten to imply later lifecycle state. Mutable tasks/checklist/state/history/review/archive outputs are not bound as future current-source invariants.",
    "Format retains existing non-executable-script warnings and release check records runtime_eval_executed=false. No paid model, runtime installation, device operation or model effectiveness/Token/cost evaluation was performed. Remote PR/main CI, protected merge, immutable Release and Root source-only promotion require their own exact-source receipts and are not pre-certified."
  ],
